# Antigravity's CLI, agy, as a kiln harness in a Shards microVM (kiln plan
# 01a1cd8e862e7169a074db3d5fa33f3d, step 26). kiln runs agy in its headless stream-json mode (Kind
# "antigravity", crates/kiln/src/harness/kinds.rs). It comes in as pin.json pins it (pin.sh checks
# each archive's SHA-512 against Google's updater, as Google's installer does) in
# ./antigravity-<arch>/: harness.json and bin/agy. Nothing else installs it, and no sign-in is in
# the image: agy keeps its own in the system's keyring, which a microVM has none of, and step 33
# brings sign-ins from outside the microVM.

# Google's static musl build of agy needs no loader or libc from the base. It checks TLS against the
# system's CA bundle and carries no roots of its own, so any base with CA certificates runs it: this
# default is step 19's, pinned by digest.
ARG BASE=buildpack-deps:trixie-scm@sha256:4f34e1d673fdb65371de9f88bdd32c4e30152fe692b35604aef5c0b3c0e6da10
FROM ${BASE}

# BuildKit sets TARGETARCH in the global scope, so the stage declares it to name each platform's
# harness directory.
ARG TARGETARCH
HARNESS antigravity FROM ./antigravity-${TARGETARCH}

# Its network reach, every part named (default deny): a network for this harness alone, which it
# joins with no flow to any member; names past the microVM through its resolver (--dns); and TCP 443
# out, opened at the network's boundary (--egress) and the microVM's (EXPOSE ... AS egress), for agy
# speaks HTTPS alone. These are the bring-up's grants (Shards' docs/examples/harness-claude) until
# step 9 grants providers by name. Nothing comes in; no other port or protocol goes out.
NETWORK --dns --egress=443/tcp provider FOR antigravity
EXPOSE --harnesses=antigravity 443/tcp AS egress FOR provider
CONNECT antigravity WITH antigravity ON provider

# The project, and the person's home. agy keeps its settings, MCP servers and conversations under
# $HOME/.gemini, and no variable of its own moves them. A harness sees the image read-only, with its
# own /tmp scratch and these volumes alone writable, so the whole home is the person's volume, and
# harness.json sets HOME=/home/antigravity: .gemini lands there, and so does what the programs agy
# runs keep in a home (.gitconfig ...), until step 7 gives every harness its home. HOME in run.env
# needs a shards at or after 997f4e47e on Shards' main (v0.8.0 is the first release with it), where
# run.env replaces init's HOME=/tmp; before it, init's came first and agy took it. harness.json also
# turns off agy's self-updater (AGY_CLI_DISABLE_AUTO_UPDATE=true: the pin is the version that runs)
# and puts caches that follow XDG's rule on the scratch (XDG_CACHE_HOME=/tmp/.cache), out of the
# person's volume. Both volumes are the harness's alone, and outside /tmp, which the scratch covers.
VOLUME --target-kind=harness /workspace FOR antigravity
VOLUME --target-kind=harness /home/antigravity FOR antigravity
